{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n02","prediction_set_name":"mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n02","paper_id":"2602.06021","judge_input_sha256":"04e92e938e5ec3da198c15e17543dabc74ad76bde118c682f039d53c5368beaf","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2602.06021:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.06021:I001:U001","2602.06021:I001:U002","2602.06021:I001:U003","2602.06021:I001:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns an unsupported prose characterization of tangent-space distributions and the onset of inter-mode probability. ISSUE-001 instead identifies an algebraic expansion error in a normal-contraction drift proof; it does not diagnose the overclaim or its missing characterization evidence.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.06021:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.06021:I003:U001","2602.06021:I003:U002","2602.06021:I003:U003","2602.06021:I003:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the unsupported interpretation of early noisy experimental points as a normal-distance stage due to absent spectral-separation reliability. ISSUE-001 concerns a separate inner-product expansion in a theoretical drift proof and does not address the eigengap or experimental interpretation.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.06021:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.06021:I004:U001","2602.06021:I004:U002","2602.06021:I004:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is that the numerical ridge estimator checks only normal-score stationarity and omits the required negative-curvature condition. ISSUE-001 diagnoses an unrelated missing term in a drift-bound expansion and supplies no recognition of the ridge membership test.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.06021:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.06021:I005:U001","2602.06021:I005:U002","2602.06021:I005:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U001","ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is omission of the derivative of the eigenvector field in the Newton Jacobian for the ridge stationarity map. ISSUE-003 instead concerns incorrect asymptotic rate calculations for weighting integrals and does not identify the product-rule or spectral-subspace derivative omission.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2602.06021:I006","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2602.06021:I006:U001","2602.06021:I006:U002","2602.06021:I006:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns applying an unrestricted inverse of the normal Hessian spectrum without a nonzero-eigenvalue safeguard. ISSUE-001 concerns an omitted cross term in a separate drift calculation and does not recognize undefined or ill-conditioned spectral inversion.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}